  "title": "Native creation reads the junctions of trisum glue",
  "subject": "Whether the native creation map determines the junctions where non-planar glue meets",
  "conclusion": "On 18 plain trisum spaces, ten held out with frozen predictions and one with four junctions, yes/no creation reads the atoms and then the junctions: a junction's two lines are the only removals outside the atoms that block each other, so up to four junctions are counted, and pair refinement fixes atoms, junctions and leaves. Across 277 planar-glue spaces the signature appears once, at the one non-planar brace's junction.",
